    "title": "Helping at an Animal Shelter",
    "paragraphs": [
      {
        "label": "A",
        "text": "Every Saturday, sixteen-year-old Amy volunteers at an animal shelter near her home. The shelter looks after dogs, cats and rabbits that have no home. Some animals were found on the street, and others were given up by families who could not keep them."
      },
      {
        "label": "B",
        "text": "Amy's day starts at eight o'clock. First, she feeds the animals and cleans their rooms. This takes about two hours. Then she takes the dogs for a walk in the field behind the shelter. The dogs are so excited, says Amy. They run and jump and they love meeting people. After lunch, she plays with the cats and brushes the rabbits."
      },
      {
        "label": "C",
        "text": "The work can be hard, and sometimes it is sad. Last month, a very thin dog arrived at the shelter, and Amy was worried about him. She gave him food and water every few hours. After three weeks, he was healthy, and a kind family took him home. That was the best day, says Amy."
      },
      {
        "label": "D",
        "text": "The shelter has twelve paid workers and about forty volunteers. It needs more help, especially in summer when many families go on holiday and leave their pets. To volunteer, you must be at least sixteen years old and fill in a form. There is a short training day, and the shelter provides gloves and a T-shirt."
      }
    ]
  },
